# Inside a try block the call ends its block and has two ways on: the return, and a rare edge to the handler. The way of the return has no test.
# The callee may have allocated, so the block polls before it leaves the handler.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="orZero" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Double b@[[doubled]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}Terminal|ExitsSideways|{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: #[[returned]], Rare:#[[caught]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[returned]]:
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK: Double b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[doubled]], 
# CHECK-NEXT: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint({{*}}Terminal|ExitsSideways{{*}}:LoopHint)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: #[[left]], Rare:#[[caught]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[left]]:
# CHECK: Return(b@[[sum]], Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[caught]]:
# CHECK: Return($0.000000(b@{{*}}), Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# CODE: f2: size={{*}} handlers=1
# The frame, the call, the addition, the poll and the return.
# X64: instructions: 4, patchpoints: 2
# ARM64: instructions: 5, patchpoints: 2
